// Type-check gate for the test suite — tests/graph, tests/utils, tests/platform
// and tests/monitor.
//
// tsconfig.json includes only ["src"] (excluding src/tui), so tests/** never
// takes part in any tsc program: `bun run typecheck` stays green while the
// tests drift away from the production contracts they exercise (Bun is
// transpile-only, so type errors never surface in `bun test` either).
//
// This config extends the repository compiler options (NodeNext + strict) and
// adds the covered test directories on top of src: tests/graph (the graph
// engine suite), tests/utils (shared helper tests such as error-text),
// tests/dsh-dispatch.test.ts — the file the graph migration forgot, whose stale
// imports no type gate saw — and, after the cleanup round that closed the last
// blind spot, the two directories that used to be compiled by nothing at all:
// tests/platform and tests/monitor.
//
// Widening to tests/platform/** + tests/monitor/** puts 54 further files in
// the program (tsc --listFiles, with versus without the two includes): 48
// `*.test.ts` files (45 under tests/platform, 3 under tests/monitor), the
// fixture tests/platform/sandbox/fixtures/browser-probe.ts, and 5
// `node_modules` `.d.ts` declarations those tests reach. It was gated on
// repairing the diagnostics those two directories carried before the
// widening — the repair round counted 70 across 12 files, 27 of them in
// tests/platform/dsh-role-switch-route.test.ts alone and 2 in
// tests/monitor/monitor-reader-graph-events.test.ts, which asserts a
// `phase_change` event the hand-written `GraphEventType` union had dropped.
// Every repair was type-level and inside the test or the fixture it builds: a
// wrong literal, a missing required field, a union member read without
// narrowing, a double whose shape did not match the port it stands in for.
// Exactly one diagnostic proved PRODUCTION incomplete instead — the dropped
// `phase_change` member of `GraphEventType`, widened type-only. The widening
// excludes no file (the exclude list below is still only src/tui) and neither
// widened directory carries a suppression directive: `grep -rn '@ts-'
// tests/platform tests/monitor` finds no match.
//
// WHAT IS STILL NOT COVERED: every other test directory — tests/cli,
// tests/hashline, tests/web, tests/dispatch, tests/loop, tests/hooks,
// tests/asset, tests/notifications, tests/core, tests/extensions, tests/memory,
// tests/tui, tests/lsp, tests/recovery, tests/integration, tests/session,
// tests/prompt, tests/signal, tests/helpers — plus the root-level
// tests/*.test.ts are still compiled by NO tsc program. On this revision they
// carry 1284 diagnostics: run the four lines below as one block from the
// repository root and take the number the last line prints (counting rule —
// tsc reports each diagnostic on one line carrying `error TS` and continues a
// longer message on indented lines that do not repeat it, so `grep -c
// 'error TS'` is the diagnostic count):
//
//   P=${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/rolebox-tsconfig-probe; mkdir -p "$P"
//   ln -sfn "$PWD/node_modules" "$P/node_modules"    # so types: ["bun-types"] resolves
//   printf '{"extends":"%s/tsconfig.json","compilerOptions":{"noEmit":true},"include":["%s/src","%s/tests/**/*.ts"],"exclude":["%s/src/tui"]}\n' "$PWD" "$PWD" "$PWD" "$PWD" > "$P/tsconfig.json"
//   bunx tsc -p "$P/tsconfig.json" 2>&1 | grep -c 'error TS'
//
// The probe config lives outside the tree: include/exclude resolve against the
// config file's own directory (hence the absolute paths) and so does the
// `types: ["bun-types"]` lookup (hence the node_modules link). Do not read this
// include list as covering tests/** as a whole.
//
// `src/tui` stays excluded. Its 127 TS2322 diagnostics are the documented
// @opentui `fg`-not-on-SpanProps false positives that scripts/build-tui.ts:35-47
// already accepts; adding it here would only reproduce a known-bad gate.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src",
    "tests/graph/**/*.ts",
    "tests/utils/**/*.ts",
    "tests/dsh-dispatch.test.ts",
    "tests/platform/**/*.ts",
    "tests/monitor/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["src/tui"]
}
